// endpoint_hold_parked_bridge.proto — HoldParkedBridge: keep a workspace
// parked at its cold gate reachable from claude.ai, and say when a prompt
// typed there arrives.
//
// WHY A PARKED SHIM HOLDS A VENDOR PROCESS AT ALL (owner ruling, 2026-11-02,
// overturning the 2026-10-27 "a gate runs no shim" ruling for this case only).
// The Remote Control bridge is the vendor CLI's own connection, so a parked
// workspace with no vendor process cannot be reached: a prompt typed on the
// phone reached nothing on this machine, and the person got no answer until
// someone answered the gate at the editor. A workspace whose remote control is
// on therefore keeps, while it is parked, ONE idle vendor process resumed on
// the parked conversation, with the bridge on.
//
// IDLE COSTS NOTHING. The process is resumed exactly as a `pay` answer resumes
// it, and no prompt is sent, so no model request is made until a prompt typed
// on claude.ai arrives (an assumption the shim logs at INFO each time it opens
// one, until a live bridge confirms it).
//
// A REMOTE PROMPT PAYS. The vendor runs a prompt typed on claude.ai the moment
// it arrives, past agent-repl's queue (owner ruling, 2026-10-31), so the cold
// read is spent then. The shim states it here (`remote_prompt`), and the daemon
// answers the gate `pay` through the one path the editor's answer takes
// (agentrepl.v1.AnswerColdGate), which records what the vendor spent: it
// retires the gate, settles the prompts held at it and marks the cache.
//
// THE ANSWER PROMOTES, IT DOES NOT RE-OPEN. The `pay` answer's StartSession
// (a resume of the same conversation with `cold_remediation` pay) is answered
// with the session this bridge already opened, and the turn the remote prompt
// started is its turn in flight. Any other StartSession on a shim holding a
// parked bridge is refused `already_started`: the caller stands the shim down
// and starts the answer on a new one.
//
// THE BRIDGE IS THE SHIM'S, THE STREAM ONLY WATCHES IT. The bridge stays open
// for the shim's life, until the answer promotes it or the shim is stood down.
// A stream opened again (a new daemon adopting the shim) is answered `opened`
// at once, and a remote prompt that arrived while no stream was open is
// stated to the next one: the arrival is a latch, never an event that a
// stream not yet open could miss. The stream ends once the bridge is
// promoted.

